      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you've reached a place of profound emptiness, and that feeling of everything collapsing is a very real, very heavy thing to carry. When the foundations of your world crumble, the silence that follows can feel like the only honest thing left. If you're feeling like nothing matters, perhaps the simplest, most immediate act of taking care of yourself—like just letting the emptiness settle—is the only thing that makes sense right now.",
